<item><title>Shipping route changes benefit Djibouti amid Red Sea crisis</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/shipping-route-changes-benefit-djibouti-amid-red-sea-crisis-662821/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/shipping-route-changes-benefit-djibouti-amid-red-sea-crisis-662821/</guid><category>Djibouti</category><description>Carriers disrupted by insecurity in the Persian Gulf are reorganising routes, while the high cost of detours is drawing some back towards Suez.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:29:56 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" length="31696" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Djibouti shows African water utilities its Doraleh desalination plant</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-shows-african-water-utilities-its-doraleh-4744e3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/dj/djibouti-shows-african-water-utilities-its-doraleh-4744e3/</guid><category>Djibouti</category><description>Djibouti depends on three sources of water: boreholes, a pipeline from Ethiopia and the Doraleh seawater plant, which sends its output to the Farah Had reservoir.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:33:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" length="31696" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/dj.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
